        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e26961a4-cd00-5fbf-81e1-dd409328874d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lawrence Turman, John Badham, S. S. Wilson, Brent Maddock, Ally Sheedy, Steve Guttenberg, Fisher Stevens, Austin Pendleton, G. W. Bailey, Tim Blaney\n- Films: The Graduate, Pretty Poison, The Great White Hope, The Thing, Mass Appeal, Short Circuit, The River Wild, American History X, Short Circuit 2\n- Organizations: University of Southern California, The Peter Stark Producing Program, Academy Awards\n- Concepts: film production, comic science fiction, military robots\n\nFacts:\n- Lawrence Turman was born on November 28, 1926, in Los Angeles.\n- Lawrence Turman is a film producer and serves as the director of The Peter Stark Producing Program at the University of Southern California.\n- Lawrence Turman was nominated for an Academy Award for The Graduate (1967).\n- Lawrence Turman produced Pretty Poison (1968).\n- Lawrence Turman produced The Great White Hope (1970).\n- Lawrence Turman produced The Thing (1982).\n- Lawrence Turman produced Mass Appeal (1984).\n- Short Circuit is a 1986 American comic science fiction film directed by John Badham and written by S. S. Wilson and Brent Maddock.\n- Lawrence Turman produced Short Circuit (1986).\n- Short Circuit stars Ally Sheedy, Steve Guttenberg, Fisher Stevens, Austin Pendleton, and G. W. Bailey, with Tim Blaney voicing the robot Johnny 5.\n- Short Circuit follows an experimental military robot that is struck by lightning, gains more humanlike intelligence, and explores its new state.\n- Short Circuit 2, a sequel to Short Circuit, was released in 1988.\n- Lawrence Turman produced The River Wild (1994).\n- Lawrence Turman produced American History X (1998).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4fad0db7-4932-5c0e-b91b-d9fa77a99650",
        "text": "Page: Lawrence Turman. Sentence: Lawrence Turman (born November 28, 1926 in Los Angeles) is a film producer who currently serves as the director of The Peter Stark Producing Program at the University of Southern California.\nPage: Lawrence Turman. Sentence: He was nominated for an Academy Award for \"The Graduate\" (1967).\nPage: Lawrence Turman. Sentence: He has also produced such films such as \"Pretty Poison\" (1968), \"The Great White Hope\" (1970), \"The Thing\" (1982), \"Mass Appeal\" (1984), \"Short Circuit\" (1986), \"The River Wild\" (1994), and \"American History X\" (1998).\nPage: Short Circuit (1986 film). Sentence: Short Circuit is a 1986 American comic science fiction film directed by John Badham and written by S. S. Wilson and Brent Maddock.\nPage: Short Circuit (1986 film). Sentence: The film's plot centers upon an experimental military robot that is struck by lightning and gains a more humanlike intelligence, with which it embarks to explore its new state.\nPage: Short Circuit (1986 film). Sentence: \"Short Circuit\" stars Ally Sheedy, Steve Guttenberg, Fisher Stevens, Austin Pendleton and G. W. Bailey, with Tim Blaney as the voice of the robot named \"Johnny 5\".\nPage: Short Circuit (1986 film). Sentence: A sequel, \"Short Circuit 2\", was released in 1988.",
